e": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le16ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two parts to the sentence.<br/><br/>   One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span>.<br/><br/>  Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">will/won't</span><br/> You use a comma after the condition in this form.   You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first. It can be in interrogative form. <br/><br/>  Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Will/Won't</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">if</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  ?"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If you don't think about your audience,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you won't engage them.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " A Short Article"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Steps to writing an article<br/><br/>  STEP 1: Choose your topic<br/><br/>  Select a topic that interests you. Think about your topic over a period of time.<br/> Write a rough draft  with everything you can think of. A rough draft is the first stage in the writing process. It is the stage where you add all your ideas together.<br/><br/>  STEP 2: ADDRESS YOUR AUDIENCE'S NEEDS.<br/><br/>  Think about your audience and how you can write the article to answer their questions.<br/><br/>  STEP 3 : DO YOUR RESEARCH<br/><br/>  Research is very important. Include:  <ul><li>Definitions</li> <li>Quotes</li> <li>Examples</li></ul><br/><br/>  Collect all the important information you need.<br/><br/>  STEP 4: TIGHTEN YOUR DRAFT.<br/><br/>  Put your rough draft and your research together. Does the information in your article blend together? Proofread your work.<br/><br/>  STEP 5<br/><br/> Read the article to a friend. <br/> Does your article:<br/> <ul><li>Include all the information?</li> <li>Is it in order logical?</li></ul><br/> Ensure that the article is checked for spelling, grammar and punctuation errors."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ambitious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "strong desire for success "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I heard you are quite ambitious."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a conversation at work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rough draft"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the first stage of writing before proofreading and adding more information "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Remember, never hand in a rough draft."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to engage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get and keep someone's attention "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  If you don't know who you are writing for, you won't engage your readers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accurate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "free from mistakes or errors "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your information will not be accurate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take someone seriously"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to trust someone's work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will not be taken seriously as a writer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write an article on a topic of your choice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose a topic you want to write about. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Decide on your audience."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Research your topic. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a 80-100 word article."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your article for spelling, grammar and punctuation errors."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your article aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write an article on a topic of my choice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I complete research on a topic online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I proofread my work. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my article to a friend."}]}], "type": "sena"}